From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: restore BSS Color Disabled when no colour change starts

hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler() sets he_bss_color_disabled
before it starts the colour change of each BSS, so that the CCA beacons
and any beacon rebuilt during the countdown carry BSS Color Disabled.
hostapd_fill_cca_settings() builds the beacons with the previous state
again, and the driver installs the CCA beacons only for a change it
starts. Where hostapd_drv_switch_color() fails, or the settings cannot
be built, for every BSS of the radio, no beacon carries the disabled
state, but the configuration keeps it: a later beacon rebuild disables
BSS Color without a colour change, and get_status reports -1 for a
colour the beacons still use.

Count the colour changes that started, and where none did, restore the
state BSS Color Disabled had before, which also resumes the ageing of
the OBSS colours that the disabled state paused.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5403,7 +5403,8 @@ void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handle
 {
 	struct hostapd_data *hapd = (struct hostapd_data *) eloop_data;
 	os_time_t delta_t;
-	unsigned int b;
+	unsigned int b, started = 0;
+	u8 was_disabled;
 	u64 avoided;
 	int i, r;
 
@@ -5421,6 +5422,7 @@ void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handle
 	 * hostapd_fill_cca_settings()) and any incidental beacon rebuild
 	 * during the CCA countdown carry the correct Disabled=1 state.
 	 */
+	was_disabled = hapd->iface->conf->he_op.he_bss_color_disabled;
 	hapd->iface->conf->he_op.he_bss_color_disabled = 1;
 	hostapd_bss_colors_in_use_update(hapd->iface);
 
@@ -5463,12 +5465,19 @@ void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handle
 		ret = hostapd_drv_switch_color(bss, &settings);
 		if (ret)
 			hostapd_cleanup_cca_params(bss);
+		else
+			started++;
 
 		free_beacon_data(&settings.beacon_cca);
 		free_beacon_data(&settings.beacon_after);
 		os_free(settings.ubpr.unsol_bcast_probe_resp_tmpl);
 	}
 
+	if (!started) {
+		hapd->iface->conf->he_op.he_bss_color_disabled = was_disabled;
+		hostapd_bss_colors_in_use_update(hapd->iface);
+	}
+
 	hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_color(hapd);
 }
 
